    "context": "Native sched_getattr query arguments and exact prefixes: 15406 root/UID1000 checks per architecture, including six PID targets, 16 sizes, 10 buffer forms,flags 0/1,ordinary/two upper PID words and upper size/flag controls. Real RR/BATCH queries and four full user-range boundary controls per cohort; native page caps 16KiB ARM/4 KiB x86. Original 3040 failures, corrected and same-ELF Linux 6.12.51 zero. Eleven probe allocas, no heap/index helpers. Two warmed 200-cycle cohorts retain flat storage. Four production captures,sole getter C scope, six-case native profiles, eight host files, unchanged allocation allowance refusals, pinned compiler/source/C/ELF inputs, executing negatives and independent lifetime review. Prior x86 reference reserved-top-page setup and earlier preflights remain separate. Setter semantics,policy/permission/races,  glibc, foreign/ELF32 and broad roadmap gates remain open",
